invariant: INV-11
file: record.c
catches: aes_suite_test
reason: rec_dir_update runs "traffic upd" at SHA256_LEN under every
  suite, so a TLS_AES_256_GCM_SHA384 direction rekeys from 32 of its 48
  secret bytes and keeps 16 stale ones. The peer derives the whole 48, so
  the first record after a KeyUpdate fails its tag. aes_suite_test
  compares the updated secret with HKDF-Expand-Label at SHA-384 over all
  48 bytes.

--- old
    size_t hash_len = suite_hash_len(d->suite);
#else
--- new
    size_t hash_len = SHA256_LEN;
#else
